		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=936#p936"><![CDATA[
Hi, I have been trying out the GE as a novice user. forgive me if I don't know enough about the GE to give useful feedback.<br>So far pretty I am impressed however I have some issues with the Audi car on the ramp.<br>In v11 if you stopped on the ramp and resumed the wheels would spin fast but you would go nowhere - same if you bumped into the vert side of the ramp -just stuck there  <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_eek.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":shock:" title="Shocked"> <br>v14 performs ok in straight motion up and back down however if you turn the car while backing down the ramp the same issue develops. Still sticks if I bump into side of ramp.<br>Would it be possible to add some slide into the cornering or if inclined? <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_cool.gif" width="15" height="15" alt="8)" title="Cool"> <br>I notice some quivering after a collapse with boxes still that although better is a little unnerving - can there be a damping control for very small motions rather than a straight cut off?<br>Anyway keep up the great work  <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=486">out of bounds</a> — Wed Apr 26, 2006 9:10 am</p><hr />
